---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT } from '../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Terms of business', url: '/terms/' }];
---

<Page
  title="Terms of Business — John Bald Funeral Directors"
  heading="Terms of business"
  description="Our terms of business, estimates, payment terms, complaints procedure and regulatory disclosures."
  standfirst="How we work, what you will be given in writing, and what to do if something goes wrong."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p>
      This page summarises how we work. Your own written estimate and confirmation of
      instructions are the documents that apply to your funeral, and they take precedence
      over anything here.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    John Bald Funeral Directors is a trading name of {SITE.parentCompany}, which also
    trades as A &amp; A Doyle in Galashiels and Herkes Funeral Directors in Gorebridge.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices and estimates</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/funeral-costs/standardised-price-list/">Standardised Price List</a> and{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-costs/additional-options-price-list/">Additional Options Price List</a>{' '}
    are published on this website, displayed in our window, and available in print, as
    required by the Funerals Market Investigation Order 2021.
  </p>
  <p>
    Before you commit to anything you will receive a written estimate itemising everything
    discussed, separating our own fees from money we pay to third parties on your behalf.
    You may take it away and think about it, and you may change your mind about any
    element.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not add a markup to third-party fees. Where those change between the estimate
    and the funeral — a crematorium fee rising, for example — we will tell you before the
    funeral rather than after.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <p>
    Our invoice is normally due within 30 days of the funeral. Where the estate is
    settling it, we will invoice the estate and wait; banks will usually release funds for
    a funeral bill ahead of anything else.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you need longer, tell us. We would far rather agree something workable than have a
    family avoid answering the telephone.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancelling or changing arrangements</h2>
  <p>
    You may change your arrangements or move to another funeral director at any point. We
    will charge only for work already done and for third-party costs already committed,
    and we will transfer everything promptly and without obstruction.
  </p>

  <h2>Funeral plans</h2>
  <p>
    We act as an introducer for Golden Charter Limited, who are authorised and regulated
    by the Financial Conduct Authority. We receive a commission for arranging a plan.{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-plans/">More about funeral plans</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Our business interests</h2>
  <p>
    We hold no ownership interest in any crematorium, cemetery or burial ground. We
    receive no payment for referring you to any minister, celebrant, florist, stonemason
    or solicitor.
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    Please tell us first, by telephoning{' '}
    <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a>, emailing{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>, or asking to speak to the
    funeral director who looked after you. Most things can be put right quickly.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we cannot resolve it, funeral directors in Scotland operate under a statutory Code
    of Practice made under the Burial and Cremation (Scotland) Act 2016, and complaints
    may be raised with the Inspector of Funeral Directors for Scotland.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    We take care to keep the information here accurate, and every guide and directory
    entry carries the date it was last checked. Fees and regulations set by councils,
    crematoria and government change, sometimes without notice — please confirm anything
    critical with us or with the relevant authority rather than relying on a web page.
  </p>
</Page>

